<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Persepolis</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Persepolis was the ceremonial capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire</a>, located in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fars">Fars</a> in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> and begun under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darius-i">Darius I</a>. Subject nations presented tribute there, as depicted in the reliefs of its palace complex. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a> occupied it and burned the palace in 330 BCE, and its administrative tablets show the influence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elamite-confederation">Elamite Confederation</a>'s bureaucracy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/persepolis.jpg" alt="Persepolis" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Laurens R. Krol · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2018-09-21_Iran,_Persepolis,_Tachara_(from_the_southeast).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
